sponux (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Searching the web. A row under the local results offers to take the query
    to your browser, and a query that names a URL ("github.com",
    "https://…") offers to open it instead. It scores below every local
    result, so it surfaces when nothing better was found rather than pushing
    anything out; "?query" asks for it outright.
  * The engine is configurable in [web], with extra ones reachable by prefix:
    "g:cats" searches whatever [web.engines] calls g. DuckDuckGo by default.
  * Nothing is sent anywhere until Enter is pressed. There are deliberately no
    live suggestions from a search engine: those would mean an HTTP request per
    keystroke, and every letter typed leaving the machine before anyone decided
    to search.
  * --check reports the engines and which browser https:// links open in.

 -- automatorn <automatorn@gmail.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 23:40:00 +0700

sponux (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opening something with an application counts as using that application.
    The editor you open every project folder with now rises in the application
    search and comes back at the top of the next "open with" list, instead of
    wherever the desktop filed it. Counted the same way for a Shift+Enter
    choice, for an [open] rule and for the desktop default.
  * Typing is faster: the installed-application list is cached instead of being
    rebuilt from GIO on every keystroke, which measured 28.5 ms per keystroke
    against 1.9 ms now, and a keystroke overall about 50 ms against 25 ms. The
    cache is dropped when an application directory changes and when a .desktop
    file is edited, so an application installed while sponux is running is
    still found without restarting it.
  * An application credited because an [open] rule or the desktop default ran
    it counts for half a use, against a whole one for an application named or
    chosen from the "open with" list: the rule was decided once and every file
    since repeats it. [rank] indirect tunes this; 1.0 counts them alike.
  * What the ranking has learned can be forgotten: Shift+Delete on the selected
    result, or --forget PATTERN and --forget --all from a terminal. Until now
    the only way out of one wrong entry was deleting the whole history.
  * --which also reports which application would open a path, and what that
    application's own history is worth to its rank.

 -- automatorn <automatorn@gmail.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 22:10:32 +0700

sponux (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New application icon, and it ships as a vector master besides the fixed
    hicolor sizes: a 256px bucket and scalable/ are installed as well, so a
    HiDPI panel no longer scales the 128px one up.

 -- automatorn <automatorn@gmail.com>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0300

sponux (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Runtime problems are recorded in ~/.local/state/sponux/sponux.log instead
    of a stderr that a hotkey-launched process does not have; the failures a
    user can act on also raise a desktop notification.
  * Ships its own icon rather than borrowing the theme's system-search.
  * --check gained three sections: which installation is answering on the
    session bus (a package and a source checkout share one name), what starts
    the daemon, and the tail of the runtime log.
  * A fresh install says what it is for: the first few opens ask for sponux to
    be bound to a key.

 -- automatorn <automatorn@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0300

sponux (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: application, file and calculator search in a resident
    GTK 4 daemon toggled over D-Bus.
  * Ships a desktop entry, a manual page, and --autostart for starting the
    daemon at login.

